## The uncomfortable part
This is the fifth same-day over-correction in a month, and the first where the over-correction was itself a *correction of an over-refutation*. The topic's own guardrail — "don't install 4.6×10⁻⁵ as the audited-correct A, that would be the mirror-image over-claim" — was the right instinct aimed one level too shallow. The mirror-image over-claim wasn't a *value* of A. It was the *existence* of ℓ.
